# **Detailed Design - Power Management and Conditioning Subsystem (PMCS)**
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Power Management and Conditioning Subsystem (PMCS) is responsible for supplying stable, uniterrupted electrical energy to all operatinal compnents and peripherals of the Telluric Current Ground Fault Indicator (TC-GFI).
Its primary function is to accept, isolate, condition, and distribute the electrical power required by the microcontroller, telecommunication module, data acquisition system (DAQ), and active analog front-end components. 
This subsystem ensures that each interanl load receives power at the correct voltage level while maintaining exceptional electrical isolation and minimal noise to protect sensitive microvolt-levle earth potential 
measurements. 

At a high level, the PMCS accepts unconditionoed power from an external 5 V DC source, such as the Voltaic Systems V75 "Always-On" recharable power bank, with axuliary off-grid charging provided by the plug in 
6 W monocrystalline solar panel. Once energy is delivered to the internal power condtioning network, it is routed through certified board-mount isolated DC_DC converter (RECOM/Murata 1W SIP4) that establishes a 
reinforced 2 kV glavanic isolation barrier. This barrier is critical to eliminate earth ground loops and protect the downstream instrumentation from the high Ground Potential Rise (GPR) and the transienet surges 
experienced when operating in high-voltage substaion enviroments.

Following isolation the power network converts and condtions energy into independent regulated digital and ultra-low-noise analog power rails using high-PSRR linear post-regulators (Analog Devices LT3042). 
These rails power all necessary computational and sensing componenets, ensuring stable voltage conditions and suppressing high-frequency switching ripple below 10&micro;V<sub>RMS even during heavy active LTE transmission 
load steps. 
